{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Concept Statement.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Concept Statement.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"concept statement concept statement","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Concept Statement.md","fileName":"Concept Statement.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Concept Statement","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 14:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Game Design Methods]] · [[Game Concept Development]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Design Methods","Game Concept Development","Game Concept Document","Game Pitch","advancedgamedesign.pdf","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Concept Statement.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Concept Statement.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"concept statement concept statement","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Concept Statement.md","fileName":"Concept Statement.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Concept Statement","heading":"Concept Statement","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A concept statement expresses a game's central experience and differentiator in one or two brief, accurate sentences. It should be short enough to remember and repeat while still communicating what the player does and why the game is distinctive.\n\nThe statement anchors a [[Game Concept Document]] and opens a [[Game Pitch]]. Refining it with other people reveals where the underlying concept is unclear or where listeners form a different mental model than intended.\n\nThe source calls this a high concept statement and limits it to roughly two or three sentences. Its job is to communicate the most important aspects quickly, leaving platform, audience, progression, and production detail to the larger concept document.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Design Methods","Ga